{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אל מוציאו ממצרים", :translit "el motzi'o mimitzrayim", :gloss "El who brings him out of Egypt"} {:he "ב\"פ", :translit "b'pe", :gloss "two times"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Phrase occurs twice in the biblical text; the doubling signals future redemption paralleling the exodus from Egypt"}], :frame {:text "The phrase \"El who brings him out of Egypt\" appears twice in Balaam's prophecies: Numbers 24:8 here and in a parallel formulation. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the repetition as a typological indicator: the exodus from Egypt serves as the paradigm for a future redemption, just as He brought them out then, so He will bring them out in the time to come.", :sources ["Numbers 24:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ועצמותיהם", :translit "v'atzmotam", :gloss "and their bones"} {:he "עי\"ן תלויה", :translit "ayin teluyah", :gloss "suspended ayin"} {:he "ז' עממים", :translit "ziv amamim", :gloss "seven nations"} {:he "ס\"ג אומות", :translit "sig umot", :gloss "sixty-three nations"} {:he "ס\"ג", :translit "sig", :gloss "sixty-three"} {:he "נאלחו", :translit "nilchu", :gloss "they were joined together"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "עצמותיהם", :b "ס\"ג"} {:kind :other, :note "Suspended ayin signals the uprooting of seven nations now and sixty-three nations in the future; combined total is sixty-three, matching the gematria of the word"}], :frame {:text "Seven Canaanite nations are enumerated in Scripture as the peoples Israel dispossesses upon entering the land (Deuteronomy 7:1). The Ba'al HaTurim links the suspended letter ayin in this word to a future uprooting of sixty-three nations, noting the gematria of עצמותיהם equals sixty-three, so that the seven and sixty-three combine to match the word's full numerical value, indicating they were all joined together.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 7:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Phrase occurs twice in the biblical text; the doubling signals future redemption paralleling